<p>President Trump, First Lady Melania Trump, Vice-President J.D. Vance, and other senior US officials were evacuated from the White House Correspondents’ Association dinner at the Washington Hilton in Washington on April 25 after a gunman fired at a security checkpoint outside the ballroom. Authorities took the suspect into custody before he reached the reception hall, and multiple outlets said President Trump and other protectees were unharmed. Officials said the suspect was carrying multiple weapons. President Trump later said a Secret Service officer was shot but protected by a bulletproof vest. US Attorney Jeanine Pirro said the suspect would face charges including assaulting a federal officer with a dangerous weapon and using a firearm during a crime of violence. Investigators were still examining the motive and whether additional charges, including possible terrorism counts, could follow. The shooting turned a high-profile evening celebrating the Washington press corps into a scene of confusion, with hundreds of guests diving under tables as armed agents entered the room. One reassuring note in an otherwise tense night was the speed of the security response: officers stopped the suspect before he entered the ballroom, the injured officer was reported to be doing well, and the event is expected to be rescheduled.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GL2r81DtBh86vx5-RJN6eIRih8yAC4-JqUrNA81zPHHS5r8pG-Wp376-H6V3CbfoJIEf5HqGQWgmYujXt0F09lTRqZzOUcbyQnWx9VVBa-LEoCD3jK5FqsHupNYjfLfAcAE0lXjwv14UY2pc4gW4jcqJyy3eC0MJdo0ibRudW2fHwttpOiF4QPzu3FjH4HSUwPH1s3vhrPSkcjqtjf5PgbNSRMbYK2IoPLaV5EI8Qou3KughouHq-EIJY02S4LdgYg' alt='Donald Trump is evacuated by the Secret Service from the White House Correspondents&#x27; Dinner at the Washington Hilton in Washington, on April 25, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Witness accounts: BBC correspondent Gary O&#x27;Donoghue and other attendees said they first mistook the sounds for dropped trays or plates before realizing shots had been fired and taking cover.</li><li>Security footage: Surveillance video released by President Trump showed the suspect running past metal detectors toward the checkpoint as security agents drew their weapons.</li><li>Event disruption: White House Correspondents’ Association chair Weijia Jiang initially said the program might continue, but later told attendees that law enforcement wanted the hotel cleared; President Trump asked for the dinner to be rescheduled within 30 days.</li><li>Hotel history: The shooting happened at the Washington Hilton, the same hotel where President Ronald Reagan was shot and wounded in 1981.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: President Trump said he believed the attacker was a &#x27;lone wolf,&#x27; praised Secret Service and law enforcement for moving quickly, and said he wanted the dinner rescheduled soon rather than canceled. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/25/trump-evacuated-from-white-house-correspondents-association-dinner-00892113'>Politico</a>)</li><li>US Attorney for DC Jeanine Pirro: Pirro said prosecutors were pursuing federal assault and firearms charges while leaving open the possibility of additional charges as the investigation develops. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/25/trump-evacuated-from-white-house-correspondents-association-dinner-00892113'>Politico</a>)</li><li>White House Correspondents’ Association: Association chair Weijia Jiang told guests that law enforcement wanted them to leave the premises and described the interruption as a reminder of both the importance and the vulnerability of First Amendment freedoms. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/25/2026/trump-evacuated-from-white-house-correspondents-association-dinner'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Attending journalists: Witnesses including Gary O&#x27;Donoghue and Wolf Blitzer described initial confusion, followed by fear once they realized an armed man was nearby and took cover under tables or on the 